# .intentfiles -- which ARTEFACTS are realised to disk (ST0057 WP-02).
#
# Two regions, and the distinction is POSITIONAL, not by content:
#
#   Outside the markers  PINS. Written by a human, survive an `intent organize`
#                        rewrite byte for byte. Pin a thread here to keep it
#                        realised after it closes -- without this the pin would
#                        vanish with the files and nothing would name the
#                        decision.
#   Inside the markers   GENERATED from current status by `intent organize`.
#                        A function of status, not a memory of what realisation
#                        last produced, so there is nothing here to go stale.
#                        A hand edit inside the markers is REVERTED, not
#                        refused, on the next run -- write it above instead.
#
# Grammar: `<SIGIL>:<ID>`, sigil in STEELTHREAD | ISSUE, optional trailing
# `# comment`. Nothing else. A line the parser cannot read ABORTS the run with
# its line number -- a skipped line drops an artefact from realisation and
# leaves an estate indistinguishable from one that never listed it.
#
# It names ARTEFACTS and never FILES. `Project::classify` stays the single
# answer to what a file IS, and the two compose: STEELTHREAD:ST0056 realises
# the thread and, through classify, whatever files it produces.

# BEGIN INTENT
# END INTENT
